|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Floating Bus Stop|Sub-chapter 19 - Floating Bus Stop]]
|money drop = 750¢ - 2,953¢
}}

==Enemy==
This enemy has powerful [[Long Distance]] attacks that can reach to 350~650, but stands at a mere 150 range, which is well within her blind spot. Dolphina also possesses 450k health and extremely fast movement speed, and is nearly always seen in groups. This may all sound insane for an enemy of this caliber, but fortunately she has 30 knockbacks.

==Strategy==
Dolphina's many knockbacks can dramatically increase her survivability, so units with high damage per hit are preferred in most stages. Use strong attackers with short enough range to enter her blind spot, like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]] or [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]]. The best strategy against Dolphina is to use "ranged meatshields" or few or no meatshields and attackers with short range or short attack animations. [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] with low range like [[Saber (Uber Rare Cat)|Saber]] should also be used with this strategy to ensure Dolphina can't hit them at all.

Rushers such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Li'l Valkyrie (Uber Rare Cat)|Wind Dancer Valkyrie]] and [[Maglev Cat]] are best used without meatshields. You can also use tanky units like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]], [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed M. Titan Cat]] to get into Dolphina's blind spot as they will take full advantage of her 30 knockbacks.

Using slow meatshields can be preferrable, but only if they are able to tank at least two hits. This stops Dolphina's attack from being triggered too quickly, similarly to a strategy used against [[Lord Gravey]] and [[Miss Haka]], and this gives your cats more time to deal damage to knock her back. If she has support enemies such as the [[Master A.]] and [[Rain D.|Rain Ds]] in [[No Return Flights]], it is best to either use mid-ranged cats with high health or spammable mid-range units so they can stack enough to prevent the Dolphinas from ever attacking, which can quickly cripple a stack of cats. [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] cats can also be very effective, as they usually can fit inside her blind spot.

