==Trivia==
*Her Japanese name, Iruka Musume (イルカ娘, "Dolphin Daughter" or "Dolphin Girl"), may be a reference to ''[[wikipedia:Squid Girl|Squid Girl]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s eponymous [[wikia:squidgirl:Squid Girl|protagonist]], whose Japanese name is Ika Musume (イカ娘, "Squid Daughter" or "Squid Girl").
*Dolphina and the first stage she appears in, [[No Return Flights]], both reference folk singer [[wikipedia:ja:イルカ (歌手)|Toshie "Iruka" Kanbe]], whose stage name means "dolphin":
**Dolphina's description pulls from the [[wikipedia:Kaguyahime (band)|Kaguyahime]] song "[https://youtu.be/3-y-VregNqg Nagoriyuki]", which was famously [https://youtu.be/FwXluXjBaqw covered] by Iruka; it mentions riding a train, a careless youth, and wasting time without realizing it. Her Japanese description even says she rode the train from Tokyo.
**No Return Flights' Japanese name, Mō Riku ni wa Kaerenai (もう陸には帰れない, "Can't Return to Land Anymore"), is a play on "[https://youtu.be/x-JJ5NJXvt4 Mō Umi ni wa Kaerenai]" (もう海には帰れない, "Can't Return to Sea Anymore").
*In [[Minna de Nyanko Daisensou]], Dolphina had a different description:

{| class="article-table mw-collapsible" border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width: 100%"
|-
!scope="row" |'''Description'''
!scope="row" |'''Translation'''
|-
|夢見ていた都会の生活に別れを告げ<br>地元での縁談で結婚を選んだイルカ。<br>フォークシンガーを目指す彼を支え続けた<br>52年間に今は微塵の未練もない。
| A dolphin who said farewell to the city life she had dreamed of<br>and chose to get married through matchmaking in her hometown.<br>She still doesn't have the slightest regret about the 52 years she's spent<br>supporting her husband as he strove to be a folk singer.
|}

*Dolphina (and possibly the whole of [[Cutpurse Coast]]) were planned for [[Version 5.10 Update|Version 5.10]], but for some reason, her enemy ID was empty.
*Along with [[Johnnyleon]], she has the lowest standing range of all [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance Enemies]].

